      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "it would be nice to know if you are using a locomotion layer which does \"temporary pose space\" whenever you are going to crouch/prone. It might be that the temporary pose space is used for the menu height while your viewpoint gets forced into the vrchat defined prone height.\nI noticed that too when i was creating my post ( https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1137-add-a-parameter-which-shows-if-the-menu-is-opened ) - shared the link since it contains a picture showing the issue",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
